# The capabilities are exactly the groups the access controls in slapd.ldif
# name, so a name outside that set is a typo. Creating it would produce a group
# no access control mentions, and the account would be refused every attribute
# the capability was meant to grant, with nothing saying why. Nothing at all is
# created: the capabilities are resolved before the account is added.
ldap_create_user --system --cn "my_service" --user-password "secret"    \
                 --capability "mail-routing-reader"

# Expected exit status: 1
# Expected error output:

Failed to create the system account "my_service".
There is no "mail-routing-reader" capability. The capabilities are the groups
named by the access controls in slapd.ldif, and are created along with the
rest of the directory by ldap_create_top_level_directory_and_system_entries.

# Expected LDIF:
